name chess-com-games
match *.pgn
# PGN packaging uses formats/pgn.format; chess.c applies the legal board rules.
# Every game is a record [line, tags, layer]: its line the trajectory of positions and moves, replayed under
# firmware/chess.firmware by the Variant it names; its tags (the players, their ratings, the clocks, the date, the result)
# as written; its clock comments ([%clk]) its layer. All of that is the game's content, and none of it is claimed of the
# game: a game is a whole record no other record is, so a claim of it could collide with none. chess.com's archive is of
# games played: a record with variations or NAGs would be an annotator's study and is said as one.
grammar pgn
records played
# Completed played games attest [position_before, canonical_move, position_after]
# with the result scored for the side making the move; * attests no outcome.
